# Whole objects: why an apple floats and a potato sinks
#
# Density belongs to the whole object. Pumice contains dense silica but its
# air-filled pores lower the stone's bulk density; an apple also carries air
# spaces. A potato is slightly denser than water. The picture and the words
# below both use those reviewed whole-object densities.
register lv1

add v1 water 250mL
add v1 apple 40g
look v1

new beaker
add v2 water 250mL
add v2 pumice 20g
look v2

new beaker
add v3 water 250mL
add v3 potato 40g
look v3

# Prediction to discuss: changing only an ingredient density would be the
# wrong calculation. Shape, pores and trapped air are part of a bulk object.
# This bounded model does not yet simulate water entering pumice pores, so the
# pumice does not slowly waterlog and sink.
